# Wolfenstein 3D shareware v1.4: the first level from the start up the main corridor, three guards
# shot, and the painting west of the corridor's top pushed into a secret room, where it moves two
# tiles. Run with --seconds 86.
#
# Turns move a few degrees a frame, so the route is fixed by walking into walls, not by angles. Ctrl
# can't be typed: the mouse button fires. The mouse is put at (160, 100) first and every click is
# there; the menus move the cursor, though, so the first click moves the mouse (and turns the player).
1000:{move 160 100}
# Menus into the game, and through the first door, as in wolf3d-first-level.inputs.
15000:{space}
27000:{space}
31000:{up}{wait 300}{up}{wait 300}{up}{wait 300}{up}{wait 300}{up}{wait 500}{enter}{wait 1500}{enter}{wait 1500}{enter}
44000:{hold up 2500}{hold space 200}{wait 1500}{hold up 1200}{hold left 700}
# North to the next door; into the corridor's west wall, back east to the door's column, open it, and
# north to the door after it.
51000:{hold up 1300}
52500:{hold left 790}
53500:{hold up 500}
54200:{hold right 1470}
56000:{hold up 210}
56500:{hold left 735}
57400:{hold space 200}
59000:{hold up 2300}
# Open it, cross the big room to the next door; turn back and shoot the patrolling guard.
61600:{hold space 200}
63300:{hold up 2000}
65500:{hold left 1000}
66700:{click 160 100}{click 160 100}{click 160 100}{click 160 100}
# Back to the door's column, open it, north to the hallway, face west and shoot the guard standing at
# the painting.
68900:{hold left 1215}
70300:{hold up 90}
70600:{hold left 735}
71600:{hold space 200}
73300:{hold up 1255}
74700:{hold left 720}
75500:{click 160 100}{click 160 100}
# West to the painting and push it; turn and shoot the guard coming from the north while the wall
# moves.
76700:{hold up 600}{hold space 200}
77700:{hold right 1290}
79100:{hold right 100}{click 160 100}{click 160 100}{click 160 100}
